# Applies to the repo-root build context, shared by two Dockerfiles now:
# uis/Dockerfile (the `ui` service, which also COPYs packages/shared) and
# services/Dockerfile (the `backend`/`worker`/`flower` services, which also
# COPY data/pipelines/weekly-location-performance — see that Dockerfile's
# own comment for why). `services` and `data` must NOT be blanket-excluded
# below — only their unneeded subpaths are.

# Generic noise, wherever it appears.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache

# Entire directories neither image needs — the Dockerfiles only COPY
# uis/brasaland-web, uis/backoffice, packages/shared, services/api, and
# data/pipelines/weekly-location-performance; everything else at root
# would otherwise bloat the build context for no reason.
docs
supabase
scripts
agents
memory-bank
skills
src
internal
mcps
workflows
infra
.claude
.devcontainer

# services/ and data/ keep almost everything out too — only the two
# subpaths services/Dockerfile actually COPYs are re-included.
services/*
!services/api
!services/Dockerfile
!services/.dockerignore

data/*
!data/pipelines

data/pipelines/*
!data/pipelines/weekly-location-performance
